Complete local PHP example; the app itself does not execute it:
```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
class Note { public string $text = 'first'; }
class Box { public function __construct(public Note $note) {} }
$first = new Box(new Note());
$second = clone $first;
$second->note->text = 'second';
echo $first->note->text, ' ', $first === $second ? 'same' : 'different', "\n";
```

Optional local transfer task: Implement __clone to clone the Note explicitly and predict first.text. You may trace it without a PHP interpreter; reading completion is not proof of a local run.

PHP invokes __clone on the new outer object after copying its properties. This no-argument hook replaces that copy’s nested Note with a cloned Note; $this is the new Box. It returns no value. The later edit therefore no longer changes first.note.
```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);
class Note { public string $text = 'first'; }
class Box {
    public function __construct(public Note $note) {}
    public function __clone(): void { $this->note = clone $this->note; }
}
$first = new Box(new Note());
$second = clone $first;
$second->note->text = 'second';
echo $first->note->text, ' ', $second->note->text, "\n";
```
Expected output: first second.

